{"availability":"available","full":"nostra-chat/nostra-chat","name":"nostra-chat","description":"Nostra.chat is a 100% client-side Progressive Web App for decentralized messaging, forked from Telegram Web K. It replaces the Telegram backend with peer-to-peer encrypted chat over Nostr relays and integrates Tor via WASM for network-level privacy. No servers, no accounts, no install — just cryptographic keys and a browser.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":5,"forks":0,"created":"2026-04-10T22:44:16Z","updated":"2026-08-06T08:34:08Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://nostra.chat/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T16:23:40.027Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T16:23:40.027Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T16:23:40.027Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T16:23:40.027Z","stars":5,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Privacy-first decentralized messaging with end-to-end encryption and anonymous relay-based delivery.","Nostra.chat is a 100% client-side Progressive Web App for decentralized messaging, forked from Telegram Web K. It replaces the Telegram backend with peer-to-peer encrypted chat over Nostr relays and integrates Tor via WASM for network-level privacy.","No central application server. No accounts. No native install. Just cryptographic keys, independent relays, optional supporting services, and a browser."],"features":["1:1 encrypted text messaging with real-time delivery over Nostr relays","Group chats up to 12 members using NIP-17 multi-recipient gift-wrap — relay operators cannot determine group membership","Encrypted photo and file sharing via Blossom blob storage (AES-256-GCM); broader video/voice interoperability remains under verification","Message deletion (local and remote via NIP-09 kind 5)","Replies, edits, and emoji reactions over the Nostra transport"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nostra-chat/nostra-chat/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3a10304e7a9de07b26c2bcd1f02d0c8da4dfb1fe45d7f46a49587fde993f641a","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T16:23:40.146Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T16:23:40.146Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Privacy-first decentralized messaging with end-to-end encryption and anonymous relay-based delivery.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nostra-chat/nostra-chat/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"SimpleX uses SMP relay servers; anyone can self-host, but most users rely on the project-operated defaults.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nostra-chat/nostra-chat/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"SimpleX has no account system — each installation is a separate identity.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nostra-chat/nostra-chat/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"The push relay is open source (nostr-webpush-relay) and operates over NIP-98-authenticated registration; users can swap the endpoint to a self-hosted instance at any time.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nostra-chat/nostra-chat/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"Nostra.chat's positioning is different: fully decentralized over Nostr relays, with user-owned keys, no account to create, censorship-resistant mirror distribution including IPFS, and zero installation — all in the browser.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nostra-chat/nostra-chat/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"3a10304e7a9de07b26c2bcd1f02d0c8da4dfb1fe45d7f46a49587fde993f641a","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nostra-chat/nostra-chat/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T16:23:40.147Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-06T08:34:08Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nostra-chat/nostra-chat/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T16:23:40.149Z","hash":"3a10304e7a9de07b26c2bcd1f02d0c8da4dfb1fe45d7f46a49587fde993f